{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Submitted a paired transfer experiment for the non-voter leadership-transfer investigation. A four-member cluster demotes one follower to non-voter and waits until that member's own configuration view reports the role; the control then calls the automatic LeadershipTransfer() and the trigger calls LeadershipTransferToServer for the demoted member on an identical cluster. The harness records the per-attempt future errors, whether the named member ever reports Leader over a three-second sample, the final leader and whether it is a voter, and one client Apply plus GetConfiguration afterwards. Local verification shows the control completing cleanly with leadership landing on another voter, while the explicit path returns 'leadership transfer in progress' on every one of five attempts across roughly a second, never installs the named member, and leaves leadership to be taken by a different voter; a client write on the eventual leader still succeeds. The control therefore isolates the failure to the explicit target path rather than to transfers on a cluster that contains a non-voter. The request declares both case events as prerequisites with role and convergence conditions, asserts future_ok on the control and target_became_leader on the trigger, uses only registered source ranges from the transfer account, states no requirement and carries no anchors, and validates against submission.schema.json.\"}"}}
